  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q20-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "20",
    "prompt": "Find a simpler expression for\n$$\\binom n0^2-\\binom n1^2+\\binom n2^2-\\binom n3^2+\\cdots+(-1)^n\\binom nn^2$$",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-q20-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "if $n$ is even.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle(-1)^{n/2}\\binom n{\\frac{n}{2}}$.\n\nEquate the coefficients of $x^n$ in $(1+x)^n(1-x)^n=(1-x^2)^n$.",
          "worked": "Let $S=\\sum_{j=0}^n(-1)^j\\binom nj^2$. Consider $(1+x)^n(1-x)^n=(1-x^2)^n$.\n\nUsing symmetry, the coefficient of $x^n$ on the left is\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\sum_{j=0}^n(-1)^j\\binom n{n-j}\\binom nj\n&=S.\n\\end{align*}$$\nSince $n$ is even, the $x^n$ term on the right comes from $(-x^2)^{n/2}$. Equating coefficients gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\nS&=(-1)^{n/2}\\binom n{n/2}.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 84
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q20-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "if $n$ is odd.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0$.\n\nThe expansion of $(1-x^2)^n$ has no odd powers of $x$.",
          "worked": "Let $S=\\sum_{j=0}^n(-1)^j\\binom nj^2$. Consider $(1+x)^n(1-x)^n=(1-x^2)^n$.\n\nUsing symmetry, the coefficient of $x^n$ on the left is\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\sum_{j=0}^n(-1)^j\\binom n{n-j}\\binom nj\n&=S.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe right-hand side contains only even powers of $x$. Since $n$ is odd, its coefficient of $x^n$ is zero. Equating coefficients gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\nS&=0.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 92
      }
    ]
  },
